# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host-side state from
# poisoning the image build.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` lands the developer's own node_modules on top of
# the tree pnpm just installed for linux. pnpm then sees a deps mismatch and
# tries to purge the modules directory, which aborts in a non-TTY step:
#   ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY
# public/ and resources/ are regenerated by `pnpm run build`; a stale local copy
# would only shadow the fresh output.

# Version control / CI
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Host installs and generated output
node_modules
**/node_modules
public
resources
.hugo_build.lock
static/css/.vite

# The example content tree is pulled by install.js, which the image build skips
# (pnpm install runs with --ignore-scripts). It is a full duplicate site.
exampleSite

# Local tooling / OS noise / alternate lockfile
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.netlify
.vercel
yarn-error.log
package-lock.json

# Not needed inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
cloudflare.md
README.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
LICENSE
